From 4f31606665b1210103755646f6e6bd99f15bc160 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crossainthero <billymillena@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:18:27 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] sarness: keep working room and the user's request through
 compaction

Compaction left a 32k local model ~5k tokens of working room (flat 16k reserve beside ~11k tokens of prompt),
kept 15k tokens verbatim (more than the room), and, because an agent run is a single user request followed by
tool rounds, summarized the request itself away. The checkpoint then called everything 'historical, not new
instructions', so the model asked what to do. Now: the reserve of a 32-64k window is the model's output limit;
the verbatim part is bounded by the budget; the user's request is always kept beside the summary and a long
single run keeps its newest steps; the checkpoint says the request is still in force; many installed skills
shrink to one sentence each (full text on demand); the auto-compaction default is the launcher's choice.
